      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Phosphocreatine (Neoton produced by \"Schapparelli Farmaceutici\") was infused intravenously to 27 patients with CHD at a dose of 2000 mg: 13 patients with unstable and 10 patients with stable angina pectoris. Phosphocreatine blocked ADP-induced platelet aggregation in these patients, but had no significant effect on the platelet aggregation induced by collagen, platelet activating factor or serotonin."},
